<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Debug on 星双</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tags/debug/</link><description>Recent content in Debug on 星双</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jzjizhe.github.io/tags/debug/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Why PIP_NO_USER=1 installs to global env</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/program/why-pip_no_user1-installs-to-global-env/</link><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/program/why-pip_no_user1-installs-to-global-env/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;strong>The note is generated by GLM5.2.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>A &lt;code>pip install&lt;/code> run inside an activated conda env kept landing in &lt;code>~/.local&lt;/code>&lt;br>
instead of the env&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code>site-packages&lt;/code>. This is what was going on.&lt;/p>
&lt;hr>
&lt;h2 id="tldr--everything-you-need-is-here">TL;DR — everything you need is here&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Symptom.&lt;/strong> Inside an activated conda env, &lt;code>pip install &amp;lt;pkg&amp;gt;&lt;/code> installs to&lt;br>
&lt;code>~/.local/lib/python3.10/site-packages&lt;/code> (shared across &lt;em>every&lt;/em> py3.10 env)&lt;br>
instead of &lt;code>envs/&amp;lt;env&amp;gt;/lib/.../site-packages&lt;/code>.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Cause.&lt;/strong> The container image exports &lt;code>PIP_NO_USER=1&lt;/code> globally. Despite the&lt;br>
name, this &lt;strong>forces&lt;/strong> user-site installs — the &lt;code>NO_&lt;/code> is ignored. &lt;code>PIP_NO_USER&lt;/code>&lt;br>
behaves &lt;strong>identically&lt;/strong> to &lt;code>PIP_USER&lt;/code>.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Fix.&lt;/strong> Any one of:
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">&lt;tr>&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">2
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">3
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#6639ba">unset&lt;/span> PIP_NO_USER &lt;span style="color:#57606a"># in ~/.bashrc (permanent, interactive shells)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#953800">PIP_NO_USER&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#0550ae">=&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#0550ae">0&lt;/span> pip install … &lt;span style="color:#57606a"># per-command&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>pip install --no-user … &lt;span style="color:#57606a"># per-command (CLI flag inverts correctly)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>Quick reference:&lt;/strong>&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>